{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "22", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "12", "M": "15", "S": "07"}}, "news": [{"title": "Register rent agreements to avoid police action, says Pune's registration department", "para": "Pune police are ramping up efforts to tackle landlords who haven't registered their rental agreements. Property owners are now required to file leave and licence agreements online, enabling tenant information updates for police records via the CCTNS system. Recently, over 175 landlords and PG operators were penalized for failing to comply. This initiative is designed to enhance tenant verification throughout the city.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/register-rent-agreements-to-avoid-police-action-says-punes-registration-department/133419658?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-137136/133419658.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Patna civic body acts on 26,746 property misuse cases", "para": "Following a Supreme Court directive pertaining to the Loganathan vs State of Tamil Nadu case, the Patna Municipal Corporation is targeting more than 26,000 cases of unauthorized construction. To ensure swift resolution, executive officers will hold periodic hearings, issuing notices to property owners in residential zones. This initiative seeks to uphold compliance and enhance living conditions for residents.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/patna-civic-body-acts-on-26746-property-misuse-cases/133419627?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-154096/133419627.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}, {"title": "Ranchi civic body orders installing rainwater harvesting structures on eligible properties", "para": "The Ranchi Municipal Corporation has taken a bold step by mandating the installation of rainwater harvesting systems for qualifying properties. These systems are essential for recharging groundwater, and property owners are obligated to set them up and maintain them properly. Those who fail to comply could face stringent administrative consequences and potential service disconnections.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/ranchi-civic-body-orders-installing-rainwater-harvesting-structures-on-eligible-properties/133419589?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-390098/133419589.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}]}